34,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The timing data shows a full pass takes over an hour and forty minutes. That's a significant time investment. Also, the outside firm requires us to tidy first, meaning outsourcing doesn't eliminate all the effort.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, the data is eye-opening! I found that some of us are barely here—one person was gone all August! Plus, only a few of us actually cook, while others just use the coffee machine. It's not balanced at all!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings confirm that our standards differ significantly; what one person considers ""done"" another might see as incomplete. Also, our past arguments in the chat always started with reminders about missed tasks. This is where the friction lies.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out we're spending about 2,300 yen a month on spray, and some things are bought twice! Also, the management cleaner is 4,200 yen an hour, but only one person gets the bill. That's confusing!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out that the bathroom grout gets dirty again in just eleven days because of the ventilation. Also, the previous tenants left a note saying they stopped talking to each other because of the cleaning. I'm... really worried about that.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Victoria, your point about differing standards explains why the time investment is so high. If we are constantly re-cleaning or over-cleaning to meet different expectations, it's inefficient. We need a concrete, agreed-upon standard to stabilize the hours.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, that's true, but we also have to address the usage! It's not fair if someone who only makes coffee and is gone for a month does the same amount of scrubbing as someone who cooks every day. We need a system that reflects actual use!","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, while usage is a factor, focusing too much on it can lead to constant monitoring and resentment. If we're always counting who used what, we might end up arguing more than we do now.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mio, @Victoria, but what about the money? We're buying things twice and only one person gets the bills! That's not fair either. We need a way to track costs so nobody is just paying for everyone else!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm scared that if we just argue about who uses what, we'll end up like the previous tenants. And the bathroom... it gets dirty so fast. Maybe we need a system that doesn't rely on us guessing?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, the grout issue suggests that some tasks require higher frequency than others. If we combine that with the timing data, it's clear that a simple rotation might be insufficient and logically flawed.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, exactly! A simple rotation is just a band-aid. If we ignore the fact that some people are barely here or barely use the kitchen, the people who are actually using the space will feel cheated. We need a flexible system!","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, flexibility can be a double-edged sword. If the rules are too fluid, we'll spend more time negotiating and monitoring each other than actually cleaning. I'm worried that ""fairness"" based on usage will just create new reasons to argue.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Victoria, but if we don't have a plan for the money, we'll argue about that instead! We need a predictable monthly cost for supplies so it's not just the person with the nearest wallet paying!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Victoria is right about the arguing. If we're always monitoring each other, it'll be stressful. But the bathroom is so unpredictable... maybe a professional could make it consistent? I just want to feel calm.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, a professional could provide consistency, but as I found, we still have to tidy up first. The real issue is the total time burden. We must decide if paying for a service is worth the remaining effort.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, it's worth it if it stops the fighting! But we still need to figure out how to split the cost and the tidying. It should be based on who's actually here and using the place!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, that's exactly my concern. Tying costs and duties to usage requires constant tracking, which often leads to the very nagging and tension I'm hoping we can avoid. We need a solution that minimizes the need for monitoring.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"@Victoria, but we can just have a fixed monthly pot! If we all put in the same amount for supplies and the cleaner, it's simple and nobody has to worry about who paid for the sponges!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I like the idea of a fixed pot. It sounds simpler. If we can just agree on a standard and have a professional help us, maybe I won't have to worry so much about the rooms.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
