60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option C is the most logical choice. Given that a full pass takes nearly two hours and our standards differ, a professional ensures consistency and reduces the time burden on all of us, provided we handle the tidying.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I like Option C too! It solves the standard problem and the time issue. But we have to agree that the cost is split based on who's actually here, not just an even split!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I strongly disagree with splitting costs by usage. That requires constant tracking and will inevitably lead to the same nagging and resentment we're trying to avoid. An even split is much more peaceful.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I agree with Victoria! An even split is way easier. If we just have a fixed monthly amount for the cleaner and the supplies, it's like a club! No more guessing who paid for the sponges!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Victoria and Rin. An even split sounds much more peaceful. If we choose Option C and keep the payments simple, maybe we can avoid the fighting and keep the rooms consistently clean.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, an even split is the only way to avoid the monitoring trap Victoria mentioned. If we spend our time auditing each other's presence, we haven't actually saved any time or mental energy. Option C with equal costs is the most efficient.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, I see your point, but it still feels wrong! If someone is gone for a whole month, why should they pay for a cleaner they didn't need? It's just not fair to the rest of us!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, fairness isn't just about the money; it's about the atmosphere in the house. If we prioritize a few thousand yen over our peace of mind, we risk the same breakdown the previous tenants experienced. Let's choose stability.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mio, but if we keep changing the price, it'll be a big mess! A fixed price is like a magic rule—everyone knows it, and nobody has to argue. Let's just make it simple and happy!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm really worried about the atmosphere too. If we keep arguing about who is here or not, it'll be stressful for everyone. I think Option C with an even split is the safest way to stay friends.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, the time we would spend calculating usage is a hidden cost. Logically, the mental burden of auditing each other is more expensive than the small financial discrepancy. Option C with an even split is the most sustainable path.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, you're all about the logic, but it's still a bummer! Still, I guess if everyone else really wants peace over pennies, I can't be the only one fighting for this. I'll go with Option C!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I appreciate your flexibility, @Mio. Choosing a path that prioritizes our relationships over perfect accounting is the best way to ensure we all feel comfortable and welcome in our home for the rest of the year.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,Yay! I'm so glad we all agree! Let's do Option C with a fixed pot for everything. It'll be so much better when we don't have to worry about who's paying for the bleach!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we could agree. I feel much better knowing we have a plan that's consistent and won't lead to fighting. I'll vote for Option C.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Since we have reached a consensus on both the method and the financial arrangement, the decision is clear. Option C provides the most rational balance of time, consistency, and interpersonal stability. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm still a little sad about the fairness part, but I love you guys and I love our home more! Let's keep it happy and stress-free. I vote for Option C!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I believe this is the most sustainable choice for our household. By removing the source of conflict and keeping the financials simple, we protect our friendship. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,"I vote for Option C! Let's make a big, happy pot of money for the cleaner and the sponges so everything is fair and clear. I'm so excited for our clean house!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I vote for Option C. Thank you for understanding. I'm looking forward to not having to worry about the rooms anymore.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
